From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm5: indexer wk+weights as one dual-store thin GEMM

VLLM_GLM5_IDX_DUAL_GEMM (default 0; read once; needs VLLM_GLM5_THIN_GEMM=1
on sm_80). Port of the "weights" part of Morrowmake's
VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_IDX_GLUE (_thin_gemm_dual_kernel, verbatim). Per MLA layer
and decode step the merged wk+weights thin GEMM, hidden.float() and the fp32
sgemm that recomputes the head weights become one launch of the same grid:
k columns stored bf16 (bitwise the merged GEMM's), weight columns stored as
fp32 accumulators (fresh mma accumulator per 64-wide k slice, Kahan split-K
reduce; not bitwise the sgemm, error bound checked by
tests/dflash2/test_idx_dual_gemm_gpu.py). Registered custom op; any call the
kernel cannot take, or an (M, N, K) first seen inside a capture, runs the
original two ops. Workspace keyed per thin_gemm.private_workspace scope with
its own tag. Warmed in kernel_warmup before capture. Off: original lines.

